///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html) and [`app_build/app.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js):\n* **Removed** the `Example:` dropdown, the `Kadane Default / Binary Search / All Positive` chips, and the `Input List: arr = [1, 3, 5, ...]` bar that was injecting unused `arr` and `target` variables into `Global Scope`.\n* **Replaced** with a single **`✏️ Paste / Edit Code`** / **`▶ Run Code`** button in the top bar.\n* **Dynamic `GOAL:` Banner**: Automatically updates to describe the classes/functions in whatever Python code you paste.\n* **Preloaded Your `Stack` Code**: Just refresh [`app_build/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html) in your browser (`F5` / `Ctrl+R`) and your `class Stack:` program will run immediately across all 45 steps!","thinking":"The \"Stack is not defined\" error likely occurred because the application was loaded directly from a local HTML file without a server. This circumvents the intended module loading setup, preventing the necessary JavaScript environment from being initialized correctly. This means the engine's required components, including the stack object, were never properly initialized.\n\n\nPreviously, the code only handled LeetCode-style standalone methods within a class, not full object-oriented programming with instance creation and method calls. Now, the execution environment has been enhanced to fully support custom class instantiation, initialization, attribute tracking, and instance method dispatch. This also includes visualizing class instances on the heap and array attributes in the memory model.\n\n\n"}
